{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014fSDLYVZvtBXPvAWu8woUd","type":"tool_result","content":"ord phrases too\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Hyphenated tool filenames (audit-regulatory-compliance.py) cannot be imported with standard `import`; use importlib.util\r\n- Tests use tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile to avoid touching actual project files\r\n\r\n## Iteration 13 - Story: US-046 Malaysian T&CM Regulatory Compliance Audit Tool\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- tuinalogy-services/_reference/regulatory-compliance-matrix.md: 4 regulations × 15 sections with keywords, required coverage, verification points\r\n- tools/audit-regulatory-compliance.py: CLI tool parsing matrix, scanning 35+ .md docs, outputting CSV with [Regulation|Section|Required Coverage|Files Addressing|Status|Recommendation]\r\n- tests/test_regulatory_audit.py: 14 pytest tests covering parse_compliance_matrix, files_matching_keywords, generate_report, write_csv\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- All 3 files were already present from a prior failed attempt (US-046 previous run)\r\n- The test file used `from audit_regulatory_compliance import ...` (underscores) but tool file uses hyphens — test was already fixed with importlib.util to load hyphenated filename\r\n- Audit result: 15/15 regulation sections Compliant, 0 Critical gaps, 0 Medium gaps\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Python cannot import modules with hyphens via normal import; must use importlib.util.spec_from_file_location\r\n- Test already had this fix in the latest version — iteration just needed to run and verify passes=True\r\n## Iteration 2 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026  1:24:59 PM\r\nCompleted: Malaysian T&CM Regulatory Compliance Audit Tool for Tuinalogy (ID: US-046) in 6m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-047 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nBased on the user story `US-047`, here is the technical brief for the implementation agent.\r\n\r\n**Clarification:** This user story does not involve a Frappe application. The tasks are confined to creating a standalone Python script and a Markdown documentation file within the existing project structure.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Technical Brief: US-047 - TCM Terminology Index**\r\n\r\n**1. Python Files to Create/Modify:**\r\n*   **Create New:** `tools/validate-terminology.py`. This is a new, standalone command-line script.\r\n*   **Modify Existing:** No existing *Python* files will be modified. The script will be used to find and report deviations in ~35 non-Python content files (`.md`, `.txt`, etc.) within the `tuinalogy-services/` directory, which will then need to be manually or programmatically corrected.\r\n\r\n**2. Frappe DocTypes / Hooks Involved:**\r\n*   None. This is not a Frappe task. The implementation should not involve any DocTypes, controllers, or framework hooks. All work is based on direct file system I/O.\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n*   **Terminology Index:** Create `tuinalogy-services/_reference/tcm-terminology-index.md`. This file will contain a single Markdown table with the columns: `[Chinese] | [English] | [Malay] | [NOSS Reference] | [Frequency]`.\r\n*   **Validation Script (`tools/validate-terminology.py`):**\r\n    *   Use Python's `argparse` to accept command-line arguments: the index file path, the content directory to scan, and an output file path.\r\n    *   Read the markdown index and parse the table to build a canonical set of allowed terms.\r\n    *   Recursively scan the content directory for files.\r\n    *   For each file, read its content and use regex to find terms that deviate from the canonical set.\r\n    *   Write any deviations found to the specified output file, including the file name and line number.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n*   **Character Encoding:** All file reading/writing must explicitly use `encoding='utf-8'` to handle Chinese and Malay characters correctly.\r\n*   **Term Normalization:** The check for \">1 character variant\" can be implemented by normalizing both the canonical term and the found term (e.g., removing all spaces and hyphens) before comparison.\r\n*   **Test Command:** The provided test command `[ ! -s term-deviations.txt ]` is for Unix-based shells. It will not work on Windows. An equivalent check will be needed if running on Windows.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13118310-105a-49a9-ac8c-a50a4d269c6c","uuid":"ac6fd14b-218e-4ea5-8197-970c0c167b97","timestamp":"2026-04-17T05:26:56.413Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ord phrases too\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Hyphenated tool filenames (audit-regulatory-compliance.py) cannot be imported with standard `import`; use importlib.util\r\n- Tests use tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile to avoid touching actual project files\r\n\r\n## Iteration 13 - Story: US-046 Malaysian T&CM Regulatory Compliance Audit Tool\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- tuinalogy-services/_reference/regulatory-compliance-matrix.md: 4 regulations × 15 sections with keywords, required coverage, verification points\r\n- tools/audit-regulatory-compliance.py: CLI tool parsing matrix, scanning 35+ .md docs, outputting CSV with [Regulation|Section|Required Coverage|Files Addressing|Status|Recommendation]\r\n- tests/test_regulatory_audit.py: 14 pytest tests covering parse_compliance_matrix, files_matching_keywords, generate_report, write_csv\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- All 3 files were already present from a prior failed attempt (US-046 previous run)\r\n- The test file used `from audit_regulatory_compliance import ...` (underscores) but tool file uses hyphens — test was already fixed with importlib.util to load hyphenated filename\r\n- Audit result: 15/15 regulation sections Compliant, 0 Critical gaps, 0 Medium gaps\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Python cannot import modules with hyphens via normal import; must use importlib.util.spec_from_file_location\r\n- Test already had this fix in the latest version — iteration just needed to run and verify passes=True\r\n## Iteration 2 - Fri, A